    {
      "title": "‘Timidity is a virus’: Paul Keating fights the fading of the light as he seeks to enshrine his legacy",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/02/timidity-is-a-virus-paul-keating-fights-the-fading-of-the-light-as-he-seeks-to-enshrine-his-legacy",
      "description": "<p>As a major new biography of the former prime minister goes on sale, he talks about meeting the Queen, Trump’s aims, and why his big vision will never fade</p><ul><li><p><strong>Get our </strong><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\"><strong>breaking news email</strong></a><strong>, </strong><a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\"><strong>free app</strong></a><strong> or </strong><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\"><strong>daily news podcast</strong></a></p></li></ul><p>Queen Elizabeth II met Paul Keating “alone, to her credit” in what the prime minister was informed was her great-great-grandmother, Queen Victoria’s, favourite room at Balmoral Castle.</p><p>“And I took some pleasure in explaining the furniture to her,” Keating recalls, an old elan breaking through.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/02/timidity-is-a-virus-paul-keating-fights-the-fading-of-the-light-as-he-seeks-to-enshrine-his-legacy\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-02T13:24:50"
    },
    {
      "title": "Fatal Sydney shooting could be another case of mistaken identity, police say",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/02/sydney-fatal-shooting-merrylands-west-possible-mistaken-identity-police-say-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>A man shot dead in Merrylands West was not known to police, in a case with similarities to Tuesday’s killing in Campbelltown</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>New South Wales police are investigating the shooting death of a man in Sydney’s west as a potential case of mistaken identity, marking the second fatal shooting incident in as many days.</p><p>Emergency services responded to reports of a shooting at a home in Merrylands West at about 3.15pm on Wednesday, where a man believed to be in his 30s sustained a gunshot wound.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/02/sydney-fatal-shooting-merrylands-west-possible-mistaken-identity-police-say-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-02T10:32:16"
    },
    {
      "title": "NSW police investigating possible mistaken identity after fatal shooting in Sydney’s west – as it happened",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/02/anthony-albanese-palau-forum-one-nation-pauline-hanson-channel-contos-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>This blog is now closed</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p><strong>Ride share driver charged on allegations of committing sexual acts during booking</strong></p><p>A ride share driver will face court in Sydney today over multiple allegations of sexual acts, including one allegedly committed in the city’s CBD last weekend.</p><p>They’re sick and tired of the feminisation of our curriculum and the lack of direction and leadership that they’re given. Maybe we should look at getting more male teachers in. That used to be an agenda. I don’t know what’s happened to that, but maybe we should have more male role models in schools.</p><p>I just know young boys often feel that they don’t get any kind of instruction, leadership. They’re not cherished there. They’re patronised.</p><p>They’re full of testosterone. … I just worry some of the solutions here don’t really understand what goes in a young boy’s mind.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/02/anthony-albanese-palau-forum-one-nation-pauline-hanson-channel-contos-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-02T08:48:17"
